1
00:04:05,454 --> 00:04:11,454
Eat better, live better & help save the planet.

2
00:08:10,909 --> 00:08:16,909
Food Choices is a documentary film directed by Michal Siewierski.

3
00:12:16,363 --> 00:12:22,363
This documentary explores the impact that food choices have on people's health,
the health of our planet and on the lives of other living species.

4
00:16:21,818 --> 00:16:27,818
And also discusses several misconceptions about food and diet.

5
00:20:27,272 --> 00:20:33,272
Self - Wellness Forum, played by Pam Popper.

6
00:24:32,727 --> 00:24:38,727
Self - Professor Emeritus of Biochemistry, played by T. Colin Campbell.

7
00:28:38,181 --> 00:28:44,181
Self - Wellness Advocate, played by Joe Cross.

8
00:32:43,636 --> 00:32:49,636
Self - Eco-Lifestyle Expert, played by Ashlee Piper.

9
00:36:49,090 --> 00:36:55,090
Self - Physician, Nutrition Expert, played by John McDougall.

10
00:40:54,545 --> 00:41:00,545
Self - NutritionFacts.org, played by Michael Greger.

11
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Ghostbusters (also known as Ghostbusters: Answer the Call) is a 2016 American
supernatural comedy film directed by Paul Feig, who co-wrote it with Katie Dippold.

12
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Starring Melissa McCarthy, Kristen Wiig, Leslie Jones, Kate McKinnon, and Chris Hemsworth, it
is a reboot of the 1984 film and the third film in the Ghostbusters franchise.

13
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
The story focuses on four eccentric women who start a ghost-catching
business in New York City after a paranormal encounter.

14
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
A third Ghostbusters film had been in various stages of development
following the release of Ghostbusters II in 1989.

15
01:01:21,818 --> 01:01:27,818
Sony Pictures rebooted the series following the death of the original cast member Harold Ramis in
2014, and because another cast member, Bill Murray, refused to commit to a sequel.

16
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
Some of the original cast and their family members make cameos in new
roles, and Ramis is commemorated in the film's closing credits.

17
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
The announcement of the female-led cast in 2015 drew a
polarized response from the public.

18
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
Ghostbusters premiered at the TCL Chinese Theatre in Los Angeles on July 9, 2016, and
was released in the United States on July 15, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

19
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
The film grossed $229 million worldwide against a $144 million production budget,
making it a box-office bomb with losses for the studio of over $70 million.

20
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
Sony abandoned plans for a sequel, opting instead to continue the
original film canon with Ghostbusters: Afterlife (2021).

21
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
The film explores themes of diet, vegetarian, vegetable, health, animal rights.
